// Title: Potential Credential Dumping Via WER
// ID: 9a4ccd1a-3526-4d99-b980-9f9c5d3a6ff3
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: @pbssubhash , Nasreddine Bencherchali
// Date: 2022-12-08
// Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1003.001
// Description: Detects potential credential dumping via Windows Error Reporting LSASS Shtinkering technique which uses the Windows Error Reporting to dump lsass
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((ParentUser containsCIS "AUTHORI" OR ParentUser containsCIS "AUTORI") AND (src.process.user containsCIS "AUTHORI" OR src.process.user containsCIS "AUTORI") AND (src.process.cmdline containsCIS " -u -p " AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS " -ip " AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS " -s ")) AND ((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\Werfault.exe") OR (OriginalFileName = "WerFault.exe"))) AND NOT ((src.process.parent.image.path = "C:\\Windows\\System32\\lsass.exe")))
